---
// promptanddone.com/free-ai-sites: the SECRETSITES pack (DM deliverable for the "free-ai-websites-tested" reel). /go/secretsites redirects here.
import PackLayout from '../layouts/PackLayout.astro';
---
<PackLayout title="3 free AI sites that feel illegal to know (tested) — Prompt & Done">
  <main>
    <header>
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/">Prompt &amp; Done</a> · SECRETSITES</p>
      <h1>3 free AI sites, no account: what we typed and what we got</h1>
      <p class="tag">We ran all three ourselves on a phone-sized browser, logged out, no card. One sentence became a photo, the photo became a moving clip, and a second sentence became a video with no photo at all.</p>
      <p class="note">Tested 7 Nov 2026. Free tiers and limits change; check the site before you rely on it. No affiliate links.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="s1">
      <h2 id="s1"><span class="n">1</span> duck.ai: OpenAI's image model, no account</h2>
      <p>DuckDuckGo's private AI chat. On the free plan, without logging in, it offers GPT-6 Luna, GPT-5.4 mini, Claude Haiku 5.5, Mistral Small 4, gpt-oss 120B and Gemma 4 31B, plus <strong>Create &amp; Edit Images</strong>. Our image came back labelled <em>GPT Image 2.5</em> in 19 seconds.</p>
      <p>Our prompt: <code>A tiny orange robot running a ramen stall in a neon night market at night, rain, cinematic photo, vertical 9:16</code></p>
      <p>Catch: the free plan has usage limits; the bigger models (Claude Sonnet, Opus, GPT-5.6) need a subscription. Chats are anonymized; DuckDuckGo says they aren't used for AI training.</p>
      <p class="label"><a href="https://duck.ai">duck.ai</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="s2">
      <h2 id="s2"><span class="n">2</span> vheer.com: make a photo move</h2>
      <p>Open <strong>Image to Video</strong>, drop in a picture, describe the motion, press Generate. We used the duck.ai photo and got a 4.7-second clip (push-in, rising steam, a little robot movement) in about 2.5 minutes. No signup, no watermark on our export.</p>
      <p>Our motion prompt: <code>The little robot lifts the noodles with chopsticks and smiles, steam rising, rain falling, neon flickers</code></p>
      <p>Catch: motion is subtle and generation took 2.5 to 4.5 minutes; accept the privacy banner first or Generate may not start.</p>
      <p class="label"><a href="https://vheer.com/app/image-to-video">vheer.com/app/image-to-video</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="s3">
      <h2 id="s3"><span class="n">3</span> raphael.app: a video from one sentence</h2>
      <p>In <strong>AI Video</strong>, pick Text to Video and 9:16, type a sentence. The free model (MiniMax H3 Turbo) made our 4-second 480p clip with no sign-up.</p>
      <p>Our prompt: <code>A tiny orange robot chef flips a glowing bowl of ramen in a rainy neon night market, steam rising, cinematic, slow push-in</code></p>
      <p>Catch: the free queue took about 13 minutes, the page warns results are temporary (keep the tab open and download), and higher-quality models are paid.</p>
      <p class="label"><a href="https://raphael.app/ai-video-generator">raphael.app/ai-video-generator</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</PackLayout>
